WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.147 --> 00:00:05.994
- Canar saying, "Do you think just

00:00:05.994 --> 00:00:08.911
"because I'm shy, I can't make it?"

00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:12.025
Canar, so obviously shy.

00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:14.612
- Do you know what, Canar?

00:00:14.612 --> 00:00:17.029
I think I said this, and I think lots

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:20.795
of great entrepreneurs are introverts.

00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:25.017
I think, you know, shy's
a relative term, isn't it?

00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:28.283
'Cause I've known really shy people

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:31.565
who have become a business owner,

00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:34.716
and they've been hugely successful,

00:00:34.716 --> 00:00:38.549
and, as time goes by,
they grow in confidence.

00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:41.381
Their shyness sort of disappears.

00:00:41.381 --> 00:00:44.037
I think you never, you never, ever

00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:46.199
get carried away with your own P.R.

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:47.749
You always keep your feet on the ground,

00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:51.539
you always keep that
great sense of humility,

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:54.669
and you really want to
be true to your idea

00:00:54.669 --> 00:00:57.098
and the purpose that you're pursuing.

00:00:57.098 --> 00:01:00.508
So I think, Canar, honestly, I think

00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:04.827
in this area, actually,
shyness can be quite a virtue,

00:01:04.827 --> 00:01:06.680
and I think with all these things,

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.891
if you are feeling particularly shy.

00:01:08.891 --> 00:01:11.632
Actually, another example.

00:01:11.632 --> 00:01:14.689
When you go up to these kind
of meetups and stuff like that,

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:17.615
Evan, I will tell ya now, I go

00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:19.912
and do loads of talks and stuff like that,

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.433
if someone comes over to talk to me,

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:24.307
I will allows talk to them.

00:01:24.307 --> 00:01:25.944
So, if you're at a meetup,

00:01:25.944 --> 00:01:29.834
and you want to kind of
zone in on one person,

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.471
get loose in your head saying,

00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:33.493
"That person wants to meet me today."

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.972
And walk up to 'em and
just introduce yourself,

00:01:35.972 --> 00:01:37.475
and you lose nothing.

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:39.500
Even if you're going to
never see that person again,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.247
you lose nothing, but
every time you do that,

00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:43.699
you lose a bit of your shyness,

00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:45.701
and you gain a bit more
of your confidence,

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:49.707
and I would advocate all
the great entrepreneurs

00:01:49.707 --> 00:01:53.335
you and I follow, they're
all super nice guys.

00:01:53.335 --> 00:01:55.524
They really are nice guys and gals,

00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:59.259
and fundamentally they all started

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:01.584
where you're probably starting today,

00:02:01.584 --> 00:02:04.503
and the good guys never
forget where they came from.

00:02:04.503 --> 00:02:06.887
In reality, we never
forget where we came from.

00:02:06.887 --> 00:02:09.775
We all started as aspiring
entrepreneurs with a dream,

00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:14.080
with an idea and an ambition,
and some of us kind of got lucky

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.579
and the cards played in our favor,

00:02:17.579 --> 00:02:21.214
but we're never, ever,
ever in reality lost

00:02:21.214 --> 00:02:24.557
that sense shyness, and I think, Evan,

00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:26.821
he looks like an amazing extrovert,

00:02:26.821 --> 00:02:29.399
but again, I'm sure in
his past had moments

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:31.407
of shyness or lacking in confidence.

00:02:31.407 --> 00:02:32.440
I certainly did.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.847
I've been to places where I've been afraid

00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:37.775
to go up and introduce myself to someone,

00:02:37.775 --> 00:02:40.446
and sometimes it sort of
either a little friend

00:02:40.446 --> 00:02:44.029
on my shoulder, or
someone in my inner self

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.504
just kicks me to say, "Go
on, introduce yourself."

00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:51.951
Don't feel any shame,
just go up and overcome,

00:02:51.951 --> 00:02:54.422
and then, the more you do
it, the more you practice,

00:02:54.422 --> 00:02:56.442
the more confident you become,

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:00.025
and, you know, Canar,
you might be the next

00:03:02.536 --> 00:03:04.287
Tony Robbins or something like that.

00:03:04.287 --> 00:03:08.203
Within you, all these guys
who go and do Ted Talks

00:03:08.203 --> 00:03:09.653
and all these sort of things,

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:13.087
if you look back at those
guys 10, 20, 30 years ago,

00:03:13.087 --> 00:03:15.582
they all started as
someone who was pretty shy,

00:03:15.582 --> 00:03:17.532
someone who probably lacked confidence,

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:20.615
and any of those people could be you.

